wash (0.9.2-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * wash-login: proxy generic ingress (/app/) through the multi-user front.
    Ingress-backed apps (vscode/code-server, any embedded web app) 404'd in
    multi-user deployments because /app/<token>/* is served by the router's
    HTTP handler, but behind wash-login the router binds no TCP (ctl-socket
    fd-handoff only). wash-login now has an authenticated /app/ route that
    resolves the session and hands the conn off (SCM_RIGHTS), staying out of
    the data path; the router's handoff is now path-aware (/app/ -> keep-alive
    http.Server over a shared ingress mux; /ws unchanged). v1 single-session.
  * no-cache headers on wash-login's unversioned shell assets (stops stale
    wash-ui.js after upgrades).
  * edit: File -> Open Folder... re-roots the left tree at a chosen dir.
  * router: terminal follows the foreground shell across stacked connections.

 -- sirmick <sirmick@gmail.com>  Sun, 21 Jun 2026 00:00:00 -0700

wash (0.9.1-4) unstable; urgency=low

  * Ship the busybox-style multi-call binary by default: one /usr/bin/wash
    dispatcher + relative wash-<app> symlinks, instead of ~28 separate binaries.
    Installed size 118M -> 21M; download 21M -> 7M. wash-login and wash-sudo
    stay real binaries (wash-login's file-caps can't be shared); wash-display
    unchanged.
  * Man pages for every applet (one source + .so redirect stubs) and a bash
    completion.
  * Correct the license metadata to AGPL-3.0+ (matches the LICENSE file; the
    old MIT declaration was wrong) and add a DEP-5 debian/copyright.
  * Reproducible builds: -buildvcs=false.

 -- sirmick <sirmick@gmail.com>  Sat, 20 Jun 2026 00:00:00 -0700

wash (0.9.1-3) unstable; urgency=low

  * wash-login: least-privilege per-session runtime dirs. The per-user
    wash-router (already setuid'd to the target user, now also granted group
    wash as a supplementary group) creates its own /run/wash/<uid>/sessions/
    and ctl socket as itself — wash-login no longer creates+chowns them (it
    has no CAP_CHOWN, so that chown failed silently and broke multi-user
    spawns). The runtime root is provisioned mode 2770 group wash (setgid) via
    RuntimeDirectory=, so ownership + group propagate with no privileged chown.
  * wash-login.service: RuntimeDirectory=wash, RuntimeDirectoryMode=2770,
    RuntimeDirectoryPreserve=yes (live sessions survive a wash-login restart).
  * wash-router: new --log-file; the router opens its own per-session log as
    the target user (owned by them, no chown).

 -- sirmick <sirmick@gmail.com>  Fri, 19 Jun 2026 20:30:00 -0700

wash (0.9.1-2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Split the multi-user front door into its own wash-login package. The core
    wash package is now just the router + apps (single-user, no system user or
    capabilities); wash-login (Depends: wash) owns the wash-system user, the
    capabilities, and the service.
  * wash-login ships an enabled systemd unit running as the unprivileged
    wash-system user, so a fresh install is reachable on 0.0.0.0:10000 out of
    the box rather than installing dormant binaries.
  * wash-login postinst creates wash-system, adds it to group `shadow` (default
    /etc/shadow auth backend), grants the binary cap_setuid,cap_setgid,cap_kill,
    and owns /etc/wash as wash-system:wash 0750 so secret.key can be written on
    first start without root.
  * Add /etc/default/wash-login: declares the cookie policy passed to
    wash-login (ships --allow-insecure-cookie for plain-HTTP LAN use; switch
    to --cookie-secure behind a TLS terminator).

 -- sirmick <sirmick@gmail.com>  Fri, 19 Jun 2026 16:45:00 -0700

wash (0.9.1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * wash-display: native X/Wayland compositor — real X11/Wayland guests run as
    wash windows (input/clipboard/popups/cursor/1080p output, subsurface
    capture + damage, chromeless CSD windows with move/resize bridges,
    shaped-popup alpha, and subsurface pointer-focus for in-window dropdowns).
  * wash-login: grant the multi-user front door its capabilities
    (cap_setuid,cap_setgid,cap_kill) at install time so a fresh package is
    multi-user-ready out of the box (best-effort; warns without aborting on
    filesystems lacking xattr support).

 -- sirmick <sirmick@gmail.com>  Fri, 19 Jun 2026 00:00:00 -0700

wash (0.9.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Hermetic native packaging: deb/rpm/apk built from a source-only tarball
    inside sanitized per-distro Docker images, across amd64/arm64/riscv64.
  * Optional wash-display compositor package (amd64/arm64) with vendored wlroots.
  * Multi-user wash-login, the background service tier (notify/bulk/priv),
    networking (wash-net/netd), storage (wash-disks), and the audio/media apps.
  * Build/test/packaging unified behind a goal-oriented `make` interface.

